import{_ as t,o as i,c as s,a5 as a}from"./chunks/framework.CsGesDJn.js";const u=JSON.parse('{"title":"Verification plan","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"feature/chat-scheduled-messages/test.md","filePath":"feature/chat-scheduled-messages/test.md"}'),n={name:"feature/chat-scheduled-messages/test.md"};function o(r,e,l,d,c,p){return i(),s("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[a('<h1 id="verification-plan" tabindex="-1">Verification plan <a class="header-anchor" href="#verification-plan" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Verification plan&quot;">​</a></h1><p>Executable QA lives only in ignored keep-local-only folders; no new tests in src.</p><ol><li><p>Migration: missing baseline, mismatched named index/validator, invalid existing schedule, duplicates and non-replica topology block safely. DRY_RUN has no writes; APPLY twice is safe. Fresh-init and migrated validators/index definitions match.</p></li><li><p>Create: plain/rich content, mention, DM/channel/thread/context; reject malformed, unsafe content, past/too-close/too-far dates, invalid zone and missing permissions. Same retry key/payload returns the original; changed payload returns conflict.</p></li><li><p>Privacy: other users/Workspaces cannot list/read/edit/cancel someone else&#39;s items. No message, unread, mention, websocket event or push is produced during scheduling.</p></li><li><p>Worker: not early; sends overdue once; current permissions/context/root checked; suspended/deactivated/deleted sender cannot deliver even with active membership; channel archive/removal/recipient removal fails safely. Temporary/rate-limit errors retry, capped attempts become FAILED. Restart/expired lease recovers pending work.</p></li><li><p>Race real Mongo workers, claim versus cancel/reschedule, expired-owner writes and rollback/uncertain commit. Exactly one stored message; SENT and notification intent commit atomically. STOMP happens only after commit and never on rollback. Unknown commit/broker outage leaves a durable broadcast intent; retry emits the existing message event and never inserts new messages/notification intents.</p></li><li><p>Web: quick presets/custom time and zone, retain failed draft, no double submit, closed idempotent responses preserve the draft and acknowledge already-sent work; Enter sends immediately, Shift+Enter/list/mention behavior preserved. Pending list/pagination/status, private ownership, time change/cancel and conflict refresh.</p></li><li><p>vi/en, light/dark, keyboard/focus and 375/768/1440 layouts. No native confirmations, no console errors, no accidental real message sends during browser QA.</p></li><li><p>Run Business compile/existing chat tests and Web type-check/build/targeted lint. Do not run sample seed, migration or scheduled delivery against shared Atlas.</p></li><li><p>Conversation notice: only the current user&#39;s PENDING/SENDING items in the selected channel/DM qualify, including its thread replies. Empty/FAILED/SENT/ CANCELLED do not display. Another conversation/user/workspace must not leak into the notice, even when more than 20 earlier items exist elsewhere. Use the earliest due item; pending overdue work says waiting and SENDING says sending. A keyboard or pointer activation opens the existing private schedule panel in one action. Create/change/cancel and background polling refresh the banner; query errors hide stale results. Check vi/en, light/dark and widths 375/768/1440 without overflow.</p></li></ol><h2 id="results-—-27-october-2026" tabindex="-1">Results — 27 October 2026 <a class="header-anchor" href="#results-—-27-october-2026" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Results — 27 October 2026&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Check</th><th>Result</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Business compile and existing test compilation</td><td>PASS: 739 main sources and 215 test sources</td></tr><tr><td>Existing chat regression tests</td><td>PASS: 36 tests</td></tr><tr><td>Service/worker smoke on disposable Mongo 7 replica set</td><td>PASS: 122 assertions</td></tr><tr><td>Migration DRY_RUN, repeated APPLY and negative preflights</td><td>PASS: 14 checks</td></tr><tr><td>Web scheduling utilities, locale keys and init/migration parity</td><td>PASS: 15 checks</td></tr><tr><td>Browser scheduling flows and layout checks</td><td>PASS: 31 checks</td></tr><tr><td>Additional keyboard menu/dialog checks</td><td>PASS: 5 checks</td></tr><tr><td>Web production build and targeted ESLint</td><td>PASS</td></tr></tbody></table><p>The Mongo smoke uses the real transaction/lease/index implementation with mocked SQL membership/account lookups, rate limiter and event broker. It covers atomic delivery/notification persistence, rollback, ambiguous commit and broadcast retry, expired owners (including an in-flight stale transaction), cancel/reschedule races, account eligibility and insert-only cancelled sample fixtures.</p><p>The browser uses mocked HTTP/STOMP in a separate QA session, not a logged-in user profile. It covers DM/channel/thread, rich mentions, failed/closed retry draft preservation, stable request identity, reschedule/cancel, privacy, history and stale revision recovery. Layout checks cover English/Vietnamese, light/dark and widths 375/768/1440; panels stay inside the viewport without horizontal overflow. No unexpected console/JavaScript errors or native dialogs were observed. Enter opens the menu, End selects the custom-time item, and Escape restores focus/preserves the draft without sending. QA waits for Radix&#39;s asynchronous focus navigation.</p><p>All database creation/APPLY/seed was confined to a labelled disposable QA replica set on local port 27029. No Atlas, business PostgreSQL data or paid AI was used. Executable QA, logs and screenshots remain excluded from Git under keep-local-only; no executable test files were added under src. This verification does not replace the real-user smoke after an operator applies the migration to the target database.</p><h2 id="conversation-notice-follow-up-—-27-october-2026" tabindex="-1">Conversation notice follow-up — 27 October 2026 <a class="header-anchor" href="#conversation-notice-follow-up-—-27-october-2026" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conversation notice follow-up — 27 October 2026&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Business compilation and 29 selected existing chat/security regression tests pass.</li><li>Real Mongo replica-set smoke now passes 136 assertions (the previous 122 plus 14 upcoming-projection checks). These cover own-author/channel/workspace scope, private-channel denial, thread inclusion beyond the first 20 workspace items, earliest ordering, closed-state exclusions, cancellation, sending and a response containing only the three declared metadata fields. Timestamp comparisons use Mongo&#39;s millisecond precision; state fixtures satisfy the existing validator.</li><li>Browser follow-up passes 27 checks: compact notice, one-action keyboard access, actual reschedule/cancel mutation invalidation, DM switching, waiting/sending, hidden stale data on failure, recovery, background polling, no sent messages or unexpected console/native-dialog errors. Twelve layout combinations pass: English/Vietnamese, light/dark, 375/768/1440; mobile banner is about 48px high.</li><li>Web production build and targeted ESLint pass; all 15 existing scheduling utility, i18n and schema-parity checks pass. Parity compares evaluated validator/index definitions, allowing formatting differences between migration and init.</li></ul><p>Only the disposable local QA database was initialized/seeded. This extension adds no collection, field, index or migration, so init/seeder need no further change. Restart Business to expose the additive upcoming endpoint; refresh Web. Existing scheduling metadata is still required. The real-user deployment smoke remains an operator step. QA scripts/logs stay ignored; reviewed screenshots and the owned QA container/browser/dev server are removed/stopped after verification.</p>',11)])])}const m=t(n,[["render",o]]);export{u as __pageData,m as default};
